# 8.4 compliance smoke (2026-08-01). TWO legs, ~300-500k, ~25 generations.
#
# THE ONE QUESTION: do generated checks that normalize before comparing now ALSO
# emit the pre-normalization values under the named keys
#   expectedNormalized= actualNormalized= expectedRaw= actualRaw=
# A prompt change can only fail by non-compliance, so compliance IS the result.
#
# LEG CHOICE: both are formatter/printer bugs, i.e. exactly the population the
# normalize instruction targets (code or formatted text). A leg whose checks are
# numeric would exercise nothing — the Raw keys are conditional on normalizing.
#   Closure-62 — LightweightMessageFormatter, the case that motivated 8.4
#   Closure-38 — CodePrinter/CodeConsumer, printed-source comparisons
#
# SECOND PURPOSE, per the revised sequence: this run's harnesses are the ONLY
# corpus in which the raw-vs-pinned comparison can be validated at all. 0 of 228
# archived cases carry a Raw key and none can — the field did not exist when they
# were recorded. So this is not a formality; it is the data.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT DO: 25 generations over two legs is not a guard population. The
# dismiss-pushing risk of the comparison is live-only and belongs to the next
# full suite, read per-event. No "guard passed" claim may rest on this run.
#
# Config matches the pair (-n 5 -m 12).
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 5 -m 12 --fuzz_timeout 20 --verify_timeout 20 --verify_relations --synthesize_relations --replay_relations_on_patched --rule_compile_repair"
CASES=(
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Jaid/Closure/patch1-Closure-62-Jaid.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/SequenceR/Closure/patch1-Closure-38-SequenceR.patch"
)
